course: dictionary
lesson: 1680
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word chorus is a good example. «The chorus of the song was the part everyone sang again.» The clue is song: a chorus is the part that repeats after each verse.
explain: The same word can also mean a group of singers. «The school chorus sang at the concert.» The clues are school and concert: this chorus is a group of people who sing together, not a part of a song.
explain: Chorus can be a verb too, something people do together. «Yes, Miss!» the class chorused. The clue is that the whole class speaks at once, so to chorus means to say something all together.
fact: Chorus can be a noun or a verb. As a noun it can be a part of a song, a group of singers, or many sounds at once.
fact: «Chorus» (noun) means the part of a song that is repeated after each verse.
fact: «Chorus» (noun) can also mean a large group of singers, like a choir.
fact: «A chorus of birds» means many birds singing at once, such as the dawn chorus at sunrise.
fact: «Chorus» (verb) means to say something all together, as in «The class chorused, Good morning!»
exercise: In «The chorus is catchy, but the drums need work», which part of a song is the chorus? | *The part that repeats after each verse | The first line of the song | The quietest part of a play | The name of the singer
exercise: «All Nature joining in a chorus of approval.» What does chorus mean here? | One person speaking very softly | A teacher giving orders | A song with lots of verses | *Many voices or sounds all at once
exercise: Find and copy the word that means to say something all together: «Yes, Miss!» the class chorused. | Miss | *chorused | Yes | class
test: «Every morning the whole class greets the teacher in a slow chorus.» What does chorus mean here? | One loud shout by the teacher | A quiet bell ringing | *All saying the same greeting together | A song with three verses
test: «In ancient Greek plays, the chorus explained the events.» What is the chorus in this sentence? | One hidden narrator | A king who ruled the city | *A group who commented on the story | The actors' costumes
exam: Which meaning fits «The dawn chorus woke the whole village»? | *Many birds singing together at sunrise | A group of singers in a theatre | A part of a song repeated after each verse | Everyone saying the same word at once
